  "text": "Details.so\nInspo\nVault\nMCP\nLIVE\nTry\n'playful services section'\nUnderstanding your query...\nGet Code\nTalk to us\nContact\nPricing\nLogin\nJoin for free\nCarousel UI\ndesign inspiration.\n\nDiscover 136+ examples from real websites.\n\nJoin for free\n6k+ members\nCarousel\nSections\nInteractions\nIndustries\nStyles\nNEW\nTODAY\nExtraordinary\n\nCarousel, Testimonial Social Proof\n\nSave\nd\nOpen Extraordinary\nGoogle Health\n\nCarousel, Features\n\nSave\nd\nOpen Google Health\nEduard Bodak\n\nCarousel, Services Features\n\nSave\nd\nOpen Eduard Bodak\nThe Romans\n\nCarousel, Media Showcase\n\nSave\nd\nOpen The Romans\nMatic\n\nCarousel, Features\n\nSave\nd\nOpen Matic\nGriflan\n\nCarousel, Testimonial Social Proof\n\nSave\nd\nOpen Griflan\nESR Bespoke\n\nCarousel, Cursor Interaction, Media Showcase\n\nSave\nd\nOpen ESR Bespoke\nVirugroup\n\nCarousel, Features\n\nSave\nd\nOpen Virugroup\nYou've seen less than 1%\n\nOne great detail can change a project. Find yours across 3,400+ examples, updated weekly.\n\nUnlock full access\nFind the right detail in minutes, not hours.\n\nPro opens the full library. Browse every category, combine filters to pinpoint exactly what you need, and save the best pieces to boards for your next project.\n\nWhat makes carousel UI feel considered?\n\n136+ handpicked examples of carousel UI design, captured from real production websites. Compare how different teams handle layout, states and micro-interactions before committing to your own approach.\n\nOpen several examples and compare the decisions that repeat. The patterns that survive different brands and layouts are usually the ones worth adapting to your own project.\n\nHow can studying these examples improve my work?\n\nThe more exceptional interfaces you study, the easier it becomes to recognize the spacing, hierarchy, motion and interaction choices that make a website feel considered.\n\nOver time, those decisions become instinct, so you can move from a blank page to a strong direction faster.\n\nWhy not just browse full websites?\n\nFull-site galleries are useful when you need broad direction. But finding one strong navigation, footer or transition means opening and scanning site after site.\n\nDetails organizes the exact parts, so you can compare relevant approaches in minutes instead of searching for hours.\n\nCan I use these ideas without copying?\n\nYes, as references, not templates. Study what makes an idea work, combine it with other references, and adapt it to the project's own content and brand.\n\nGreat work is not copied from one source. It is assembled from many good decisions.\n\nIs Pro worth it if I build websites regularly?\n\nProbably. One useful layout or interaction can save hours of searching and help turn an average project into one that feels considered.\n\nPro gives you the full library and everything added each week.\n\nReady to explore the full library?\nUpgrade to Pro\nExplore related categories\nButton\nList\nRows\n3D\nModal\nCard\nAccordion\nOverview\nInspiration\nVault\nPricing\nContact\nAffiliate\nLegal\nPrivacy\nTerms\nReferral\nCookies\nImprint\nSocials\nNEW\nX\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nStay ahead\n\nGet curated UI inspiration, interactions, and resources directly in your inbox.\n\nSubscribe\n\nBuilt for those who\ncare about the details.\nMade in Switzerland\n\nCurated for the world",
